KG42.register("rules-11cb83d37c803835c5f8bd2d",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R018","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R018","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Local VCG transaction prices determine the payment and receipt rates: trading buyers pay max(S^P, B_(γ+1)^P), while trading sellers receive min(S_(γ+1)^P, B_γ^P). Scope: VCG payment rules reviewed for local P2P energy trading; buyer and seller rates are distinct. The market operator must subsidize the deficit between buyer payments and seller receipts to facilitate the transaction. Scope: Financing the payment deficit in VCG transactions. Condition: The price trading buyers pay is less than the price trading sellers receive.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R018-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R018-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R018-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Financing the payment deficit in VCG transactions. | VCG payment rules reviewed for local P2P energy trading; buyer and seller rates are distinct.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R018-T01","symbol":"B_{\\gamma}^P","meaning":"Bid price at the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ (marginal bid); appears in the VCG seller receipt term $\\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P, B_{\\gamma}^P)$ and in the natural-ordering relation $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq B_{\\gamma+1}^P$.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"$/kWh","indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R018-T02","symbol":"B_{\\gamma+1}^P","meaning":"Bid price following the largest breakeven index (index $\\gamma+1$); used in the VCG buyer payment term $\\max(S^P, B_{\\gamma+1}^P)$.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"$/kWh","indices":["\\gamma+1"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R018-T03","symbol":"S_{\\gamma+1}^P","meaning":"Ask price following the largest breakeven index (index $\\gamma+1$); used in the VCG seller receipt term $\\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P, B_{\\gamma}^P)$.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"$/kWh","indices":["\\gamma+1"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R018-T04","symbol":"S^P","meaning":"Ask price printed without a subscript in the VCG buyer payment term of Table 1; the source does not index it in that term (index flagged as unresolved).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"$/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R018-T05","symbol":"\\gamma","meaning":"The largest breakeven index; it selects the marginal local bid/ask prices used by the VCG payment and receipt rates.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\gamma"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R018-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Local VCG transaction prices determine the payment and receipt rates: trading buyers pay max(S^P, B_(γ+1)^P), while trading sellers receive min(S_(γ+1)^P, B_γ^P). Scope: VCG payment rules reviewed for local P2P energy trading; buyer and seller rates are distinct.","expression":"\\text{buyer payment rate} = \\max(S^P,\\, B_{\\gamma+1}^P), \\qquad \\text{seller receipt rate} = \\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P,\\, B_{\\gamma}^P)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R018-T01","v141-c-R018-T02","v141-c-R018-T03","v141-c-R018-T04"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R018-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The market operator must subsidize the deficit between buyer payments and seller receipts to facilitate the transaction. Scope: Financing the payment deficit in VCG transactions. Condition: The price trading buyers pay is less than the price trading sellers receive.","expression":"\\text{deficit} = \\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P,\\, B_{\\gamma}^P) - \\max(S^P,\\, B_{\\gamma+1}^P) > 0, \\quad \\text{subsidized by the market operator}","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R018-T01","v141-c-R018-T02","v141-c-R018-T03","v141-c-R018-T04"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. VCG | Price trading buyers pay: $\\max(S^P, B_{\\gamma+1}^P)$ | Price trading sellers receive: $\\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P, B_{\\gamma}^P)$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"J. Lin, et al. and S P are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, re- 2. spectively.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The Vickrey-Clark-Groves (VCG) mechanism is an alternative auction mechanism that maximizes social welfare and motivates participants to bid truthfully at the expense of the market operator [46]. $B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ are the bid and ask prices following the largest breakeven index, respectively. Effectively, $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P \\leq S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ due to the natural ordering rule for sorting offers. Since the price that trading buyers pay is less than the price that trading sellers receive, there exists a deficit that needs to be subsidized by the market operator to facilitate the transaction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This settlement rule determines per-unit payment and receipt rates as functions of the fixed bid/ask prices at the breakeven index; it contains no design selection and no operational decision variable (the rates are determined by the VCG payment rule, not chosen). The design choices of this mechanism (e.g., the parameter k for the k-DA mechanisms) are not part of VCG settlement, and no decision object appears in this rule's frozen V/E.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-05","quote":"VCG | Price trading buyers pay: $\\max(S^P, B_{\\gamma+1}^P)$ | Price trading sellers receive: $\\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P, B_{\\gamma}^P)$"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-07","quote":"Since the price that trading buyers pay is less than the price that trading sellers receive, there exists a deficit that needs to be subsidized by the market operator to facilitate the transaction."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a6c6b96b5cbb28b5356fd1fdcc52231e36ba2ed51f41b86ce2ce19c575b593fb","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Rule v141-c-R018 (VCG market payment, mechanism v141-a-M03) carries explicit source math. v141-b-g01-ev-05 (Table 1) states the trading-buyer payment $\\max(S^P, B_{\\gamma+1}^P)$ and the trading-seller receipt $\\min(S_{\\gamma+1}^P, B_{\\gamma}^P)$; v141-b-g01-ev-07 states the deficit condition (buyer pays less than sellers receive) and the market operator's obligation to subsidize that deficit, together with the notation that $B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ are the prices following the largest breakeven index. Both frozen constraints C001 and C002 are retained verbatim (id, statement, role, members, original evidence) and enriched with formal expressions over the bid/ask prices at the breakeven index. The bid/ask prices and the breakeven index are fixed inputs at the settlement stage, so they are parameters (theta); the rule determines payment/receipt rates rather than choosing a design or operational decision, so x is empty. The buyer-payment term prints $S^P$ unindexed, which the page-3 text leaves unresolved; the expression copies the printed symbol and the ambiguity is logged for B re-extraction. This output relies on unreviewed candidate B evidence and does not assert that B transcription or downstream science passed independent source review.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-T01","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"$B_{\\gamma}^P$ is a local transaction bid price (pricing.local) that enters the VCG seller receipt rate at settlement.payment, so it attaches to the frozen pricing.local -> settlement.payment link E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-T02","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"$B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ is a local transaction bid price (pricing.local) that enters the VCG buyer payment rate at settlement.payment, attaching to E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-T03","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"$S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ is a local transaction ask price (pricing.local) that enters the VCG seller receipt rate at settlement.payment, attaching to E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-T04","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"$S^P$ is the (unindexed) local ask price printed in the VCG buyer payment term; as a pricing.local price feeding the settlement.payment rate it attaches to E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-T05","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"$\\gamma$ is the largest breakeven index that selects the marginal local bid/ask prices (pricing.local) used by the VCG payment and receipt rates, which reach settlement.payment through E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E002"],"rationale":"C001 states the VCG buyer payment and seller receipt rates as functions of the local bid/ask prices; it instantiates the frozen pricing.local -> settlement.payment link E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R018-E001"],"rationale":"C002 states the market operator's obligation to subsidize the deficit arising from the settlement payment rates; it instantiates the frozen coordination.local_operator -> settlement.payment link E001."}],"revision_requests":["B re-extraction (notation): verify whether the VCG buyer-payment term in Table 1 (v141-b-g01-ev-05) is $\\max(S^P, B_{\\gamma+1}^P)$ with an unindexed $S^P$, or whether that ask term should carry the breakeven subscript $S_{\\gamma}^P$. The supporting page-3 text (v141-b-g01-ev-07) defines only $B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ as the prices following the largest breakeven index, leaving the index of $S^P$ unresolved; no source-independent reading is assumed here.","B re-extraction (quantity): the source states that a deficit 'needs to be subsidized by the market operator' but gives no explicit formula or symbol for the deficit/subsidy amount. As frozen, only the inequality condition can be transcribed; if the deficit is to be a first-class quantity, C.1 would need a node (e.g., an operator subsidy quantity) and edge.","Scope check: the natural-ordering relations $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P \\leq S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ cited in v141-b-g01-ev-07 are not represented in this rule's frozen V/E and were intentionally not imported, since they are clearing/bidding properties of M03 rather than settlement-payment relations."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
